led-over-alleged-racial-harassment-elderwood-agrees-to-a-450000-settlement/articleshow/136155710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T08:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155854,imgsize-1779438.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elise Stefanik family’s DC home sells for $2.9m cash after failing to fetch $1.99m, flagged as unusual]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171929.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a notable real estate transaction, a Washington home belonging to US Congresswoman Elise Stefanik's family was sold for a substantial $2.9 million in June. This sale came after an earlier unsuccessful attempt to sell at $1.99 million. City tax officials raised eyebrows regarding the deal's unusual price point. The buyer, AFS Real Estate Holdings, remains shrouded in mystery regarding its ownership.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-home-owned-by-us-congresswoman-elise-stefaniks-family-failed-to-sell-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-home-owned-by-us-congresswoman-elise-stefaniks-family-failed-to-sell-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:04:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172299,imgsize-1186721.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lululemon founder Chip Wilson says Canadian women aren't having as many babies as men want; some men may need to import brides from Thailand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136172138.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:31:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172168,imgsize-49148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bournemouth residents oppose two new padel courts, citing noise and swearing from existing courts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171836.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Residents near West Hants Club are voicing opposition to proposed new padel courts due to existing noise issues. They report constant disturbances from shouts and sounds that disrupt their daily lives and enjoyment of outdoor spaces. Complaints have been made to BCP Council regarding noise levels and offensive language from players. The club claims it operates responsibly, with measures to manage noise and ensure member behavior.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:00:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171911,imgsize-2211641.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egypt highway inferno kills 30 after fuel tanker overturns]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171820.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A harrowing event unfolded in Giza's Al-Warraq district when a vehicle turned over and burst into flames. Tragically, over 30 individuals perished, while another 21 suffered injuries. Emergency services quickly arrived at the scene to extinguish the blaze and offer medical assistance. The incident took place on a major ring road in Greater Cairo, raising renewed concerns about the pressing issues of road safety in Egypt.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:56:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171841,imgsize-238834.cms"/></item></channel></rss>